generateGrammar -- generate a grammar file from a template
**********************************************************

  * Usage: 
        generateGrammar(template, outfile, demarkf)
        generateGrammar(outfile, demarkf)
  * Inputs:
      * template, a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, the filename of the
        template file;
      * outfile, a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, the filename of the
        output file;
      * demarkf, a *note function: (Macaulay2Doc)Function,, how to demark a
        list of symbols;

Description
===========

This method generates a grammar file for use in syntax highlighting Macaulay2
code in a text editor or web browser.

The file template may contain any of the following special strings:

  * @M2BANNER@, for placing a banner mentioning that the resulting file was
    automatically generated.
  * @M2VERSION@, for the current version of Macaulay2.
  * @M2SYMBOLS@, for a list of all Macaulay2 symbols, e.g., for automatic
    completion.
  * @M2KEYWORDS@, for a list of Macaulay2 keywords.
  * @M2DATATYPES@, for a list of Macaulay2 types.
  * @M2FUNCTIONS@, for a list of Macaulay2 functions.
  * @M2CONSTANTS@, for a list of Macaulay2 symbols and packages.
  * @M2STRINGS@, for a regular expression that matches Macaulay2 strings.

The function demarkf indicates how the elements of each of the lists will be
demarked in the resulting file.   The file outfile will then be generated,
replacing each of these strings as indicated above.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : outfile = temporaryFileName()                                           |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = /tmp/M2-30819-0/0                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : template = outfile | ".in"                                              |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = /tmp/M2-30819-0/0.in                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : template << "@M2BANNER@" << endl << endl;                               |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : template << "This is an example file for the generateGrammar method!";  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : template << endl;                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : template << "String regex: @M2STRINGS@" << endl;                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : template << "List of keywords: {" << endl;                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : template << "    @M2KEYWORDS@" << endl;                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : template << "}" << endl << close;                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : get template                                                           |
|                                                                             |
|o10 = @M2BANNER@                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|      This is an example file for the generateGrammar method!                |
|      String regex: @M2STRINGS@                                              |
|      List of keywords: {                                                    |
|          @M2KEYWORDS@                                                       |
|      }                                                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i11 : generateGrammar(template, outfile, x -> demark(",\n    ", x))          |
